FIPS-VARIANT: refuse circl's own (non Go-FIPS-module) cryptography in FIPS 140 mode.

Every gated entry point calls internal/fipsgate: in FIPS 140 mode
(crypto/fips140.Enabled) it returns the API's error ("<pkg>: use of <algo> is
not allowed in FIPS 140 mode") or, when the API has no error result, panics
with it. Outside FIPS 140 mode behaviour is unchanged.

Gated primitives:
  dh/x25519 (X25519), dh/x448 (X448), dh/curve4q, dh/csidh, dh/sidh + SIKE,
  cipher/ascon, xof/k12 (KangarooTwelve), xof BLAKE2X/K12 IDs,
  sign/ed25519 and sign/ed448 (circl's own implementations), sign/dilithium,
  sign/eddilithium2/3, sign/mldsa (circl's ML-DSA), sign/slhdsa (circl's SLH-DSA),
  sign/bls + ecc/bls12381 pairing, abe/cpabe/tkn20,
  kem/kyber, kem/mlkem (circl's ML-KEM), kem/sike, kem/frodo, kem/xwing,
  kem/hybrid, pke/kyber, hpke X25519/X448 KEMs, hybrid KEMs and ChaCha20-Poly1305,
  group ristretto255 (and oprf/ot built on it).
group P-384 uses the standard library's curve in FIPS 140 mode instead of
circl's ecc/p384. Not gated: SHA-2/SHA-3/SHAKE, HKDF, AES-GCM, P-256/384/521
ECDH/ECDSA-based hpke and oprf, RSA blind signatures and threshold RSA.

